1
00:00:06,430 --> 00:00:08,029
Chemi, could you take this, please?

2
00:00:08,029 --> 00:00:09,830
I spent all night writing it.

3
00:00:09,830 --> 00:00:10,930
I want you to read it.

4
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:12,300
Okay.

5
00:00:12,770 --> 00:00:15,430
I'm not sure you won't hurt my brother again.

6
00:00:15,430 --> 00:00:17,300
Do I really look that bad to you?

7
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:21,900
He's not picking up. I've called ten times.

8
00:00:27,070 --> 00:00:28,000
I'm his brother.

9
00:00:28,930 --> 00:00:30,430
I have a right to worry.

10
00:00:30,430 --> 00:00:33,930
If you want me in it, you have to cast someone close to me too.

11
00:00:33,930 --> 00:00:36,030
Your co-star is Din.

12
00:00:39,870 --> 00:00:41,770
Go tell him now. I'll be your co-star.

13
00:00:41,770 --> 00:00:42,700
Bro...

14
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:44,500
I'll give you another chance.

15
00:00:46,370 --> 00:00:47,930
It's only been one day.

16
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:50,800
I waited four years for you.

17
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:53,370
Take good care of me.

18
00:00:53,930 --> 00:00:56,530
I know what you're thinking, Rei.

19
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,700
But you're really just a big brother to me.

20
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:00,630
I get it.

21
00:01:00,930 --> 00:01:01,900
I'll head home.

22
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:03,130
Din,

23
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:04,900
I have feelings for you.

24
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:07,030
I have feelings for you too.

25
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:09,800
I love doing nice things for you.

26
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:11,600
Keep up the quality, okay?

27
00:01:12,130 --> 00:01:12,930
Hello, Mii.

28
00:01:14,030 --> 00:01:15,170
Come out and see me.

29
00:01:16,370 --> 00:01:17,470
I need to talk to you.

30
00:01:40,930 --> 00:01:42,400
So what now, Mii?

31
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:44,470
Do you know who Rei's hitting on now?

32
00:01:44,470 --> 00:01:47,570
He's hitting on everyone. Get a grip, Mii.

33
00:02:00,270 --> 00:02:01,970
Why'd you call me here, Aof?

34
00:02:07,170 --> 00:02:08,770
If you won't talk, I'm leaving.

35
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:12,830
It's about Rei.

36
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:16,570
Rei's been hitting on a junior at my school.

37
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:21,000
But he doesn't seem interested.

38
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,500
Tomorrow at school, I'll talk to him for you.

39
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:25,600
And I'll let you know what I find out.

40
00:02:29,530 --> 00:02:30,370
Mii.

41
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:32,730
Mii, just break up with Rei.

42
00:02:35,630 --> 00:02:37,370
Don't put up with a guy like him.

43
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:42,530
I'm going to break up with him, but...

44
00:02:42,530 --> 00:02:45,530
Just one last time. Really, just once.

45
00:02:45,530 --> 00:02:47,030
Mii, how many times now?

46
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:53,230
I'm saying this because I care about you, Mii.

47
00:04:57,830 --> 00:04:59,300
Didn't I ask you before?

48
00:04:59,300 --> 00:05:01,800
If you didn't love me, just break up with me.

49
00:05:01,800 --> 00:05:02,900
Be straight with me.

50
00:05:02,900 --> 00:05:04,230
And you cheated on me.

51
00:05:04,230 --> 00:05:05,370
How could you do this?

52
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:13,070
Answer me! Say something!

53
00:05:13,070 --> 00:05:14,500
Answer me, Rei!

54
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:19,630
I'm sorry.

55
00:05:20,700 --> 00:05:22,700
But I'm the one who hurt you.

56
00:05:24,330 --> 00:05:25,630
So you choose.

57
00:05:26,230 --> 00:05:27,330
What's it going to be?

58
00:05:38,700 --> 00:05:39,830
Disgusting.

59
00:05:41,530 --> 00:05:43,500
You know you're a total scumbag?

60
00:05:43,500 --> 00:05:46,970
You come into my life, cheat on me, and then tell me to choose?

61
00:05:47,770 --> 00:05:49,900
Why didn't you just break up with me?

62
00:05:51,330 --> 00:05:52,130
Huh?!

63
00:05:55,870 --> 00:05:57,130
Scared?

64
00:06:06,670 --> 00:06:09,470
I hope I never have to see your face again.

65
00:06:47,970 --> 00:06:49,130
Hey, Star.

66
00:06:49,730 --> 00:06:51,030
We're out of staples.

67
00:06:51,030 --> 00:06:53,800
We need to buy more or we won't finish today.

68
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:55,400
Yeah, wanna go buy some?

69
00:06:56,270 --> 00:07:01,430
Or how about we borrow staples from the guys building the stage set?

70
00:07:04,870 --> 00:07:07,500
Hm, you really want to go?

71
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:09,500
Fine, let's go together.

72
00:07:10,870 --> 00:07:13,370
I doubt it's just about the staples.

73
00:07:14,030 --> 00:07:17,030
From the looks of it, you just want to see Din, right?

74
00:07:19,830 --> 00:07:22,030
Go, go. Get there and back fast.

75
00:07:22,030 --> 00:07:23,570
Fine, I'll go. I'll go.

76
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:35,930
Uh, the popcorn cart goes at Booth One.

77
00:07:35,930 --> 00:07:37,370
Careful setting it up.

78
00:07:58,230 --> 00:08:00,870
I brought you pink milk. Your favorite.

79
00:08:03,530 --> 00:08:06,070
The event's coming up. We won't make it in time.

80
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:09,500
Hey, trust me. We'll make it. You've got me.

81
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:19,900
It's going slow because you keep fussing over me.

82
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:23,470
Oh, come on. Here, have a drink. Go on, take a break.

83
00:08:36,100 --> 00:08:37,070
Action!

84
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:50,470
Why do you follow me so?

85
00:08:51,970 --> 00:08:53,700
For I caught a god's scent.

86
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:55,130
Well, I am a god.

87
00:08:59,170 --> 00:09:02,230
My lord, I have a question.

88
00:09:03,500 --> 00:09:07,200
Just now, I saw two humans touch their mouths together.

89
00:09:07,200 --> 00:09:08,570
What was that, my lord?

90
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:13,670
It is one way humans show love.

91
00:09:13,670 --> 00:09:16,070
If one day you love someone dearly,

92
00:09:17,100 --> 00:09:19,930
you may show it in the same way.

93
00:09:21,170 --> 00:09:23,370
On to the kiss scene. Action!

94
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:53,070
My lord, then I...

95
00:10:03,100 --> 00:10:05,100
I don't think we need to really kiss.

96
00:10:05,100 --> 00:10:06,970
Is there another way?

97
00:10:06,970 --> 00:10:08,430
I don't want to actually kiss.

98
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:14,100
I don't think it'll look convincing.

99
00:10:14,100 --> 00:10:16,100
Because in a stage play,

100
00:10:16,100 --> 00:10:17,970
the audience sees from every angle.

101
00:10:18,400 --> 00:10:21,400
It's not like film or TV, where camera angles can fake it.

102
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:23,000
Hmm.

103
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:25,000
I agree with Kim.

104
00:10:25,670 --> 00:10:26,670
Honestly...

105
00:10:26,670 --> 00:10:29,330
We all want this to be the best it can be, right?

106
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,230
Right, Fuen?

107
00:10:32,970 --> 00:10:34,700
If Fuen and Din agree,

108
00:10:36,870 --> 00:10:38,070
as actors,

109
00:10:38,930 --> 00:10:41,230
they should give it their all, right?

110
00:10:43,870 --> 00:10:45,630
And me, as the audience?

111
00:10:46,300 --> 00:10:47,670
I'm totally fine with it.

112
00:10:53,900 --> 00:10:56,200
Go into the kiss scene. Action!

113
00:10:58,400 --> 00:10:59,300
Din.

114
00:11:00,730 --> 00:11:02,100
Kiss for real.

115
00:11:03,470 --> 00:11:05,330
Mm, okay.

116
00:11:18,770 --> 00:11:21,630
My lord, then I...

117
00:11:30,900 --> 00:11:32,100
Din!

118
00:11:44,770 --> 00:11:47,070
Can I borrow the stapler?

119
00:11:47,930 --> 00:11:49,270
Sure.

120
00:11:56,600 --> 00:12:00,470
Star!

121
00:12:03,300 --> 00:12:04,500
Dude.

122
00:12:05,030 --> 00:12:08,270
It's fine. We haven't finished rehearsing.

123
00:12:11,770 --> 00:12:13,830
Let's finish rehearsing first.

124
00:12:17,600 --> 00:12:21,930
Oh, hey, we've all been rehearsing for a while now.

125
00:12:21,930 --> 00:12:23,230
Is everyone hungry?

126
00:12:23,470 --> 00:12:25,200
Hungry? Anyone hungry?

127
00:12:25,530 --> 00:12:26,430
Yes, starving!

128
00:12:26,770 --> 00:12:27,600
Then...

129
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:28,630
Hey, I think...

130
00:12:29,470 --> 00:12:30,500
Mm.

131
00:12:31,770 --> 00:12:34,330
We've been rehearsing for hours, Kim.

132
00:12:34,770 --> 00:12:37,470
I think we should take a little break.

133
00:12:38,830 --> 00:12:39,830
Okay.

134
00:12:39,830 --> 00:12:40,930
Let's eat, then.

135
00:12:42,670 --> 00:12:43,500
Okay.

136
00:12:44,270 --> 00:12:45,030
Tell them, then.

137
00:12:46,070 --> 00:12:47,730
Okay, everyone, time to eat!

138
00:12:47,730 --> 00:12:49,300
Go on, go eat, guys.

139
00:12:50,100 --> 00:12:50,730
Okay, okay.

140
00:12:50,730 --> 00:12:52,530
Wow, great job! Awesome!

141
00:12:52,530 --> 00:12:53,600
Thanks, man.

142
00:13:04,530 --> 00:13:06,730
Star, wait! Wait, Star!

143
00:13:07,270 --> 00:13:08,330
Are you okay?

144
00:13:12,830 --> 00:13:15,670
Booboo, I shouldn't have walked off like that.

145
00:13:16,030 --> 00:13:18,830
Din was just rehearsing. Or am I being silly?

146
00:13:19,170 --> 00:13:20,970
Hey, no. / You're fine.

147
00:13:20,970 --> 00:13:24,330
It's normal to feel that. Din didn't tell you first, right?

148
00:13:24,900 --> 00:13:28,070
True. If you'd known beforehand, this wouldn't have happened.

149
00:13:28,070 --> 00:13:30,030
That was one hell of a surprise.

150
00:13:30,900 --> 00:13:32,070
It's fine, guys.

151
00:13:32,070 --> 00:13:35,200
Or should I just go back to Din?

152
00:13:35,770 --> 00:13:37,130
Mm, good idea.

153
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:50,570
Can I talk to you for a bit?

154
00:14:14,030 --> 00:14:15,300
What?

155
00:14:15,870 --> 00:14:17,200
I'm okay with it.

156
00:14:17,200 --> 00:14:18,230
Let's go all in.

157
00:14:18,430 --> 00:14:19,470
You sure?

158
00:14:21,130 --> 00:14:21,830
Mm.

159
00:14:27,830 --> 00:14:28,800
I'm sure.

160
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:36,770
Acting.

161
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,470
Let's just call it acting.

162
00:14:42,830 --> 00:14:43,630
Mm.

163
00:14:44,570 --> 00:14:46,600
Of course it's acting.

164
00:15:00,130 --> 00:15:01,600
Din.

165
00:15:02,170 --> 00:15:04,900
I'm sorry for walking out like that.

166
00:15:06,430 --> 00:15:08,300
Did I make you feel bad?

167
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:10,000
Not at all.

168
00:15:10,470 --> 00:15:12,500
I was more worried you'd get the wrong idea.

169
00:15:14,200 --> 00:15:18,570
Fuen and I are really just following the script. There's nothing more to it.

170
00:15:19,500 --> 00:15:20,900
I understand.

171
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:24,230
So don't worry about me, okay?

172
00:15:24,230 --> 00:15:26,230
Go back to your rehearsal.

173
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:29,930
You're sure you're really okay?

174
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:35,670
I'm sure.

175
00:15:37,530 --> 00:15:41,030
Then on the day, save me a seat, okay?

176
00:15:41,670 --> 00:15:43,670
I want to see you show off your acting.

177
00:15:45,970 --> 00:15:50,670
And... when it comes to that scene...

178
00:15:51,470 --> 00:15:55,100
Just a peck. Nothing more.

179
00:15:55,530 --> 00:15:57,970
Okay. Just a little peck.

180
00:16:09,270 --> 00:16:10,770
Our friends are adorable.

181
00:16:10,770 --> 00:16:12,830
We should cast them all in the play.

182
00:16:15,330 --> 00:16:16,830
Right. / Right.

183
00:16:18,970 --> 00:16:21,500
Star, I need to talk to you.

184
00:16:21,500 --> 00:16:23,070
What do you want with Star?

185
00:16:23,070 --> 00:16:24,730
I'm talking to him. Stay out of it.

186
00:16:27,900 --> 00:16:30,230
It is my business. I'm trying to win Star over.

187
00:16:30,570 --> 00:16:31,600
What?!

188
00:16:40,630 --> 00:16:42,070
Shit.

189
00:16:42,070 --> 00:16:43,700
Where the hell do I even start?

190
00:16:44,130 --> 00:16:46,230
Star, I'll get straight to the point.

191
00:16:46,230 --> 00:16:48,070
I've never thought badly of you.

192
00:16:49,270 --> 00:16:51,130
But what's going on with you and Rei?

193
00:17:03,970 --> 00:17:06,069
Rei and I really aren't anything.

194
00:17:07,170 --> 00:17:08,930
I don't even like him.

195
00:17:08,930 --> 00:17:11,099
But yesterday at Siam, I saw you hugging him.

196
00:17:20,329 --> 00:17:24,329
Aof, that thing at Siam was just an accident.

197
00:17:24,329 --> 00:17:27,970
Rei was just catching me. I was about to fall.

198
00:17:39,770 --> 00:17:41,970
Is there something I should know?

199
00:17:42,530 --> 00:17:43,930
It's a long story.

200
00:17:44,270 --> 00:17:45,400
It's about Mii.

201
00:17:46,370 --> 00:17:47,730
I'm not sure about Rei.

202
00:17:47,730 --> 00:17:49,530
So I came to check with Star.

203
00:17:49,930 --> 00:17:52,470
I knew it. Star wouldn't go for a guy like that.

204
00:17:53,900 --> 00:17:55,730
I'm so damn worried about Mii.

205
00:17:55,930 --> 00:17:58,430
No idea how she's doing. She won't answer my calls.

206
00:18:06,330 --> 00:18:08,000
You're sure it was just an accident?

207
00:18:09,430 --> 00:18:10,600
Yes.

208
00:18:50,570 --> 00:18:51,570
Hello, Aof.

209
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:54,270
Hello, Mii. How are you?

210
00:18:55,700 --> 00:18:59,970
I'm okay, I guess. I broke up with him.

211
00:19:01,400 --> 00:19:04,070
I don't know how I put up with him for so long.

212
00:19:06,130 --> 00:19:07,570
I feel so relieved now.

213
00:19:09,070 --> 00:19:14,170
Mm, good. If anything's bothering you, just tell me.

214
00:19:17,570 --> 00:19:18,370
Mm.

215
00:19:18,800 --> 00:19:21,070
I'm with a lot of friends right now.

216
00:19:21,530 --> 00:19:22,670
It's fine.

217
00:19:23,570 --> 00:19:26,170
But if I really can't take it,

218
00:19:26,900 --> 00:19:28,670
can you pull me back, Aof?

219
00:19:31,430 --> 00:19:32,330
Of course.

220
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:34,630
Thanks.

221
00:19:35,270 --> 00:19:36,970
Mii, let's go to Siam.

222
00:19:37,730 --> 00:19:40,600
Aof, I'll go now. Heading to Siam. Bye.

223
00:19:40,600 --> 00:19:42,000
You take care too, Mii.

224
00:19:42,570 --> 00:19:44,670
Message me anytime if anything comes up.

225
00:20:02,770 --> 00:20:04,230
You're sure about this setlist?

226
00:20:08,030 --> 00:20:13,070
I was thinking, if we swap this song with this one,

227
00:20:13,070 --> 00:20:16,130
it might open better, and feel fresh for everyone.

228
00:20:16,700 --> 00:20:17,730
What do you think?

229
00:20:18,670 --> 00:20:20,900
Shall we try running it once?

230
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:23,200
Sure. / Let's see if it works.

231
00:20:23,200 --> 00:20:24,500
Okay, everyone, places.

232
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:40,430
♪ Have you ever felt it — no matter how far the days carry us ♪

233
00:20:40,430 --> 00:20:44,370
♪ Every time I think back on those nights, on the story of that day ♪

234
00:20:44,370 --> 00:20:50,800
♪ it warms my heart all over again ♪

235
00:20:52,030 --> 00:20:58,030
♪ Looking at the photos some nights before I sleep, I smile to myself ♪

236
00:20:58,030 --> 00:21:01,700
♪ Every time I think back on those nights, on you and me ♪

237
00:21:01,700 --> 00:21:06,430
♪ a time I've never once forgotten ♪

238
00:21:09,630 --> 00:21:16,370
♪ However long the years run on, my heart still won't forget ♪

239
00:21:18,130 --> 00:21:25,370
♪ Even if we had to part in the end, that time is still just as it was ♪

240
00:21:25,370 --> 00:21:29,270
♪ It's all still so clear inside me ♪

241
00:21:29,270 --> 00:21:33,570
♪ I still remember all our good times, just the same ♪

242
00:21:33,570 --> 00:21:37,770
♪ The days we smiled at each other, the days we were close ♪

243
00:21:37,770 --> 00:21:42,630
♪ None of it has ever gone away ♪

244
00:21:42,630 --> 00:21:46,630
♪ It's all still so clear, it never faded ♪

245
00:21:46,630 --> 00:21:50,800
♪ Even if today we have to go our separate ways ♪

246
00:21:50,800 --> 00:21:55,370
♪ However far apart you and I may be ♪

247
00:21:55,370 --> 00:21:59,930
♪ our time together is still here in my heart ♪

248
00:21:59,930 --> 00:22:03,200
♪ It's all still so clear ♪

249
00:22:09,530 --> 00:22:12,930
Thank you so much to the crew and everyone today.

250
00:22:12,930 --> 00:22:16,730
That's a wrap for today. And don't forget to study your lines.

251
00:22:22,130 --> 00:22:24,930
Stage crew, you can bring the set up now.

252
00:22:33,430 --> 00:22:35,330
How you doing? / Nervous, obviously.

253
00:22:36,300 --> 00:22:37,500
You okay?

254
00:22:37,970 --> 00:22:39,970
Go home and get some rest.

255
00:22:42,170 --> 00:22:43,200
Hey!

256
00:22:47,630 --> 00:22:49,330
Hey! Get over here, quick!

257
00:22:50,800 --> 00:22:51,830
Are you okay?

258
00:22:53,070 --> 00:22:53,930
You alright?

259
00:22:53,930 --> 00:22:54,700
Physics!

260
00:22:57,800 --> 00:22:58,870
Easy, get up slowly.

261
00:23:00,370 --> 00:23:01,400
Are you hurt?

262
00:23:01,400 --> 00:23:02,570
No, no, it's nothing.

263
00:23:02,570 --> 00:23:04,070
I'm okay. It's fine, it's fine.

264
00:23:04,470 --> 00:23:05,330
Let me see.

265
00:23:05,930 --> 00:23:06,870
Ow! / Oops!

266
00:23:07,300 --> 00:23:08,370
Fine? Seriously?

267
00:23:08,370 --> 00:23:10,170
Come on, to the nurse's office.

268
00:23:12,370 --> 00:23:13,370
I'm so sorry.

269
00:23:14,300 --> 00:23:15,300
It's okay.

270
00:23:17,470 --> 00:23:19,400
You guys need to be more careful!

271
00:23:24,130 --> 00:23:25,400
Let's go.

272
00:23:26,730 --> 00:23:28,270
I'll walk you there.

273
00:23:34,300 --> 00:23:35,130
